    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362-a1">

                <pb facs="0839" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg743"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                        845.—Translation.]</seg><lb/><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Patria
                        of <date calendar="gregorian" when="1878-11-19">November 19,
                        1878</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Yesterday, at the hour when we were writing our daily, a body of about 80 men,
                    tied one to the other and conducted by several guards, passed through our
                    street. The public said that they were volunteer soldiers.</p>
                <p>Will the Diario have the kindness to tell us the cause of this impressment to
                    which those <hi rendition="#italic">galley slaves</hi> were going, and why they
                    were going?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
